            <div xml:id="d556">

                <pb facs="0746" n="632" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg632"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.51/1554: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hood</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-09-27T15:00:00-00:44"><hi rendition="#italic">September 27,
                                1922—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 4:50 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>33. About $40,000 of hut tax coming in has given temporary relief and crisis is
                    at least postponed.</p>
                <p>Liberian Government anxious to know when the Senate will adjourn <hi
                        rendition="#italic">sine die</hi> and whether there is definite reason to
                    believe Liberian loan bill be acted upon before final adjournment of this
                    session.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hood</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
